    <text>
        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="la" resp="#AV">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><persName type="divine" key="spesAugusta"><name><unclear>Spe</unclear>i</name> <name><expan><abbr>Aug</abbr><ex>ustae</ex></expan></name></persName>
                    <lb n="2"/><persName type="attested"><name><gap reason="lost" atLeast="1" atMost="3" unit="character"/></name> <name>Auconius</name>
                    <lb n="3"/><name>Optatus</name></persName> <expan><abbr>eq</abbr><ex>uo</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>p</abbr><ex>ublico</ex></expan>
                    <lb n="4"/><expan><abbr>dec</abbr><ex>urio</ex></expan> et <num value="2"><hi rend="supraline">II</hi></num>vir <placeName type="attested"><name><expan><abbr>Cl</abbr><ex>audiae</ex></expan></name> <name><expan><abbr>Ag</abbr><ex>uonti</ex></expan></name></placeName>
                    <lb n="5"/>pro salute
                    <lb n="6"/><persName type="attested"><name><expan><abbr>T</abbr><ex>iti</ex></expan></name> <name>Auconi</name> <name>Optati</name></persName>
                    <lb n="7"/>fili sui <expan><abbr>equit</abbr><ex>i</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>Rom</abbr><ex>ani</ex></expan>
                    <lb n="8"/><expan><abbr>v</abbr><ex>otum</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>s</abbr><ex>olvit</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>l</abbr><ex>ibens</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>m</abbr><ex>erito</ex></expan>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    <app><note>Text adapted from EDR, with comparison with photograph</note></app>
                    <app loc="1"><note>Line 1 appears – on the basis of photographs on Lupa – to now be entirely lost, but we have recorded here the version provided in EDR</note></app>
                    <app loc="8"><note>While EDR provides [v(otum) s(olvit)] l(ibens) m(erito), the photograph suggests that all four letters of the abbreviation are visible on the stone.</note></app>
                </listApp>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>To Spes Augusta. [-] Auconius Optatius, [holder of] the public horse, a decurion and duovir of Claudia Aguntum, for the safety of his son, Titus Auconius Optatus, a Roman knight, gladly and deservedly fulfilled this vow.</p>
            </div>
